$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: template-website/winning-trimming-com-au/hostinger-deploy
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-08"
summary: >-
  Production deployment to Hostinger VPS (VM 1607392, IP 187.77.152.132) via Docker Compose +
  Traefik. GitHub Actions CI/CD (deploy.yml) builds on the VPS via SSH, runs next build in a sidecar
  container with DB access, builds the Docker image, and restarts the stack with --env-file
  .env.production. Media files persist in a Docker volume mounted at /app/public/media (Payload
  staticDir), surviving container rebuilds.
$system: template-website/system
$service: template-website/winning-trimming-com-au
intent: >-
  Go live with the production site so customers can browse the SEO matrix, submit quotes, and staff
  can manage bookings via the Payload admin panel. Automated via GitHub Actions on push to main.
status: built
flows:
  - description: Prepare the VPS, create production compose config, and push the code.
    id: prep-and-deploy
    name: Pre-deploy preparation
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: snapshot
        target: Take a VPS snapshot before deploying
      - id: s2
        action: create
        target: Create docker-compose.prod.yml with Traefik labels, production env, and built image
      - id: s3
        action: create
        target: Create .env.production with all production credentials
      - id: s4
        action: build
        target: Build the production Docker image on the VPS
      - id: s5
        action: start
        target: Start containers with docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d
  - description: Update GoDaddy DNS to point winningtrimming.com.au to the VPS.
    id: dns-update
    name: Update GoDaddy DNS
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: get
        target: Fetch current DNS records for winningtrimming.com.au via GoDaddy API
      - id: s2
        action: update
        target: Update A record @ to 187.77.152.132
      - id: s3
        action: update
        target: Update A record www to 187.77.152.132
      - id: s4
        action: preserve
        target: Preserve MX records (Google Workspace) and TXT records (SPF, domain verification)
      - id: s5
        action: wait
        target: Wait for DNS propagation (TTL 600s, should be under 10 minutes)
  - description: Run database migration and seed the database.
    id: migrate-and-seed
    name: Database migration and seed
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: run
        target: Run pnpm migrate inside the web container to apply all migrations
      - id: s2
        action: navigate
        target: Visit https://winningtrimming.com.au/admin and create the first admin user
      - id: s3
        action: run
        target: Run the seed endpoint to populate pages, posts, projects, matrix, regions, suburbs
      - id: s4
        action: run
        target: Run the empty-pillars seed script to create caravan/trade/commercial asset types
      - id: s5
        action: run
        target: Run the Google reviews sync script to fetch reviews from Places API
  - description: Configure the daily cron job for Google reviews sync.
    id: cron-setup
    name: Configure reviews cron
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: create
        target: Create cron entry on VPS for daily reviews sync at 6am
      - id: s2
        action: create
        target: Ensure environment variables are available to cron
  - description: Verify the site is live and all pages return 200.
    id: verify
    name: Post-deploy verification
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: check
        target: curl https://winningtrimming.com.au returns 200
      - id: s2
        action: check
        target: curl https://winningtrimming.com.au/quote returns 200
      - id: s3
        action: check
        target: curl https://winningtrimming.com.au/admin returns 200
      - id: s4
        action: check
        target: curl https://winningtrimming.com.au/marine returns 200
      - id: s5
        action: check
        target: curl https://winningtrimming.com.au/sitemap.xml returns 200
      - id: s6
        action: check
        target: Verify SSL certificate is valid
contracts:
  - description: Production docker-compose.yml on the VPS with Postgres, Next.js app, and Traefik routing
    id: docker-compose-prod
    must_have:
      - Postgres 16 service with persistent volume
      - Web service built from Dockerfile.prod
      - Traefik labels for winningtrimming.com.au with SSL
      - POSTGRES_URI uses Docker service name db
      - Compose launched with --env-file .env.production so interpolation resolves correctly
      - Storage volume mounted at /app/public/media (Payload staticDir) not /app/storage
      - Media files persist across container rebuilds via Docker volume
  - description: Media files (seed images + uploads) persist across container rebuilds
    id: media-persistence
    must_have:
      - Docker volume winningtrimming_storage mounted at /app/public/media
      - Volume pre-populated with all seed media from local public/media tar
      - Payload Media collection staticDir = public/media matches the volume mount
      - New uploads survive docker compose down/up
  - description: Next.js build runs on the VPS in a sidecar container with DB access for SSG
    id: build-on-vps
    must_have:
      - Build container joins the compose network to reach db service
      - DB migration prompt (batch=-1) must not block the build
      - .next/BUILD_ID exists after build before image is built
      - Dockerfile.prod COPYs the pre-built .next into the image
  - description: GitHub Actions CI/CD for automated deploys
    id: github-actions-cicd
    must_have:
      - "deploy.yml: SSH into VPS, pull latest, build, restart, health check"
      - "ci.yml: lint + typecheck on PRs"
      - "Secrets: VPS_HOST, VPS_USER, VPS_SSH_KEY, VPS_PROJECT_DIR"
      - "--env-file .env.production used for all compose commands"
  - description: Traefik handles HTTPS with Let's Encrypt for winningtrimming.com.au
    id: ssl-cert
    must_have:
      - Traefik ACME configuration for Let's Encrypt
      - Automatic redirect from HTTP to HTTPS
      - Certificate auto-renewal
  - description: Site is accessible and all pages return 200
    id: verify-live
    must_have:
      - https://winningtrimming.com.au returns 200
      - https://winningtrimming.com.au/admin returns 200
      - All 276 media files return 200 via /api/media/file/
      - Homepage, quote, admin, pillar pages return 200
tests:
  - id: home-page-live
    setup:
      url: https://winningtrimming.com.au
    expect:
      - result: "200"
  - id: admin-accessible
    setup:
      url: https://winningtrimming.com.au/admin
    expect:
      - result: "200"
  - id: quote-form-live
    setup:
      url: https://winningtrimming.com.au/quote
    expect:
      - result: "200"
  - id: matrix-live
    setup:
      url: https://winningtrimming.com.au/marine/yachts
    expect:
      - result: "200"
  - id: ssl-valid
    setup:
      domain: winningtrimming.com.au
    expect:
      - result: valid-cert
  - id: db-migrated
    setup:
      check: migration-status
    expect:
      - count: 9
        result: migrations-applied
  - id: dns-points-to-vps
    setup:
      check: dig A record
    expect:
      - result: 187.77.152.132
  - id: mx-preserved
    setup:
      check: dig MX record
    expect:
      - result: aspmx.l.google.com
  - id: sitemap-live
    setup:
      url: https://winningtrimming.com.au/sitemap.xml
    expect:
      - result: "200"
  - id: llms-txt-live
    setup:
      url: https://winningtrimming.com.au/llms.txt
    expect:
      - result: "200"
decisions:
  - id: use-existing-vps
    decision: Deploy to existing Hostinger VPS (VM 1607392) rather than a new VPS
    rationale: >-
      The existing VPS has Docker and Traefik already configured, 4 CPU and 16GB RAM which is
      sufficient, and is already running at 187.77.152.132. No need to provision new infrastructure.
    date: "2026-09-07"
  - id: traefik-for-ssl
    decision: Use Traefik for reverse proxy and SSL rather than nginx or Caddy
    rationale: >-
      Traefik is already installed on the VPS (Ubuntu 24.04 with Docker and Traefik template). It
      handles automatic Let's Encrypt certificates and routing via Docker labels.
    date: "2026-09-07"
  - id: godaddy-dns-only
    decision: Update GoDaddy DNS A record to point to VPS rather than transferring nameservers
    rationale: >-
      Domain uses GoDaddy nameservers. Only the A record needs to change from Squarespace IPs to the
      VPS IP. MX records for Google Workspace must be preserved.
    date: "2026-09-07"
  - id: prod-compose-separate
    decision: Use a production docker-compose.yml separate from the local dev compose
    rationale: >-
      Production needs Traefik labels, production env, no volume bind mounts, and built image.
      Keeping it separate avoids dev config in production.
    date: "2026-09-07"
  - id: manual-migration
    decision: Run database migration and seed manually on first deploy
    rationale: >-
      Migration and seed are one-time operations. Manual control ensures they run exactly once,
      avoiding data loss.
    date: "2026-09-07"
